> > By default the MCMC will monitor the parameters (aka top-level nodes), not the latent states.
> >
> > You can also set the monitors when you call configureMCMC.
> >
> > Note there is also a second set of monitors, called monitors2, which can have a separate thinning interval.  This is handy when you want to monitor latent states but they are very large.
